# Full Set of Modularization and Refactor Rules

1. Do not change any UI/UX or functionality.
2. Use a Feature-Based folder structure: organize by feature, not by file type.
3. Split big components (>300 lines) and components doing multiple jobs.
4. Move constants into constants.js inside the feature.
5. Move helper functions into helpers.js inside the feature.
6. Move shared constants and helpers into common/constants.js and common/utils/.
7. Move custom hooks into hooks/ inside the feature.
8. Move Context/Providers into contexts/ inside the feature.
9. Move API calls into services/ inside the feature.
10. Group and clean up imports: libraries first, UI components next, hooks, then helpers/constants, then styles/assets.
11. Move reusable components like Button, Skeleton to common/components/.
12. Use absolute imports if possible.
13. Create barrel index.js files for clean imports.
14. Format code using Prettier after refactor.
15. Remove all unused variables and commented-out code.
